From f26d51199b579ecaf7bca86e44441b98754ea950 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Kleber <26285351+kleberbaum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:48:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] feat(plugin): hand the store to the plugins through the
 context

The ports of EssentialsX and LuckPerms keep their data in the store,
but the runtime gives a plugin no way to reach it, so every port would
need a handle of its own from the program, and nothing would make sure
that the changes of the plugins reach the file before the JVM ends.

The runtime now holds the store that the program gives it with
Runtime::set_store and hands it to every call through Context::store,
so a plugin reaches it the way it reaches the game. Once every plugin
saw ServerStopped, the last event of the server thread, where a wait
for the disk costs no tick, the runtime flushes the store, outside the
budget of every plugin, so a stop that no close follows, such as a kill
of a JVM that a thread of a mod keeps alive, loses no change.

